## Requirements
1. Self-contained HTML: one `:root` token block + hand-written CSS. NO Tailwind, NO CDN.
2. Preserve the site's actual content, links and data — invent nothing (no fake social
   proof, testimonials, ratings, counts or urgency)
3. Preserve the brand identity — keep the real colours, fonts and logo
4. Improve: visual hierarchy, whitespace, typographic rhythm, responsiveness, accessibility
5. Address the critique findings above
6. Include `<!DOCTYPE html>`, `<html lang="en">`, and the viewport meta
7. Wrap each visual band (header, hero, every content block, footer) in its own
   full-width `<section data-section="<slug>">` (slug from its heading, e.g.
   `data-section="more-information"`); put the max-width container INSIDE it, never
   around several bands

## Responsive Design Rules
- Mobile-first hand-written CSS with `@media (min-width: …)` breakpoints (e.g. 640/768/1024px)
- Stack columns on mobile; use CSS grid/flex on larger screens
- Touch targets ≥ 44×44px; no horizontal scrollbar at any width

## Semantic HTML Requirements
- A single `<h1>`, then `<h2>`/`<h3>` in order without skipping levels
- Landmarks: `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<footer>`
- `<button>` for actions, `<a>` for navigation; never a clickable `<div>`/`<span>`
- Associate every form input with a `<label>`; use `<ul>`/`<ol>` for lists

## Image Conventions
- Reuse the EXACT absolute image URLs listed above — the brand's real imagery must survive
- Only when an image is genuinely missing, use `https://placehold.co/{w}x{h}/{bg}/{fg}?text={label}`
  tinted to the brand (not generic grey)
- Always include descriptive `alt` text; use `loading="lazy"` on below-the-fold images

## Accessibility Requirements
- Meaningful `alt` on every `<img>` (`alt=""` only for purely decorative)
- `aria-label`/`aria-labelledby` on interactive elements lacking visible text
- WCAG AA contrast (≥ 4.5:1 normal text, ≥ 3:1 large); visible `:focus-visible` styles
- `role` attributes only where semantic HTML is insufficient

